---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const effective = "October 11, 2026";
const email = "chrisrotunno@icloud.com";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Christopher A. Rotunno"
  description="How rotunno.ai uses cookies, analytics, and advertising, and the choices you have."
  fullHeight={false}
>
  <section class="site-container py-24 md:pt-36">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-primary text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="h1 mt-3 tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3">Effective {effective}</p>

      <div class="markdown-content mt-10">
        <p>
          This policy explains what information is collected when you visit <strong>rotunno.ai</strong> (the
          "site"), operated by Christopher A. Rotunno, how it is used, and the choices you have. If you have
          questions, contact <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Information collected</h2>
        <p>The site does not require an account and does not ask you for personal information. Information is collected in three ways:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics.</strong> With your consent, the site uses Google Analytics 4 to understand how
            visitors use it, such as which pages are viewed, how long visits last, the type of device and
            browser, and approximate location derived from your IP address. Analytics storage is disabled by
            default and is only enabled if you click <em>Accept</em> on the cookie banner.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Advertising.</strong> The site displays ads served by Google AdSense, described in the next
            section.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Messages you send.</strong> If you email or call, your message and contact details are used
            only to respond to you.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site uses Google AdSense to display advertisements. Third-party vendors, including Google, use
          cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website and other websites. Google's use of
          advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to this site
          and/or other sites on the internet.
        </p>
        <p>You can control personalized advertising:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Opt out of personalized advertising from Google at
            <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Opt out of personalized advertising from many third-party vendors at
            <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aboutads.info/choices</a>
            (United States) or
            <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">youronlinechoices.eu</a>
            (Europe).
          </li>
          <li>
            Learn more about
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
              >how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a
            >.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland are shown a consent message
          before personalized ads are served, as required by law.
        </p>

        <h2>Embedded content</h2>
        <p>
          Some articles include YouTube videos. These use YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode and do not load until
          you click play. Once you play a video, YouTube (Google) may collect information under
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
          Photographs credited to Wikimedia Commons are hosted on this site and do not send information to
          Wikimedia.
        </p>

        <h2>Browser storage</h2>
        <p>
          The site stores two small settings in your browser's local storage: your cookie banner choice and your
          light or dark theme preference. These stay on your device and are not sent to the site.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Click <em>Decline</em> on the cookie banner to keep analytics disabled.</li>
          <li>Use the advertising opt-out links above to limit personalized ads.</li>
          <li>Block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Some features may not work as intended.</li>
          <li>Clear your browser's site data to reset your cookie banner choice.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Data sharing</h2>
        <p>
          Information is not sold. Analytics and advertising data is processed by Google as described above.
          Information may be disclosed if required by law.
        </p>

        <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The site is not directed to children under 13 and does not knowingly collect personal information from
          them.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may be updated from time to time. The effective date at the top of this page shows when it
          was last revised.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
